From c8ecdd9fc49588de98bd62206070d5ab192a9c32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clear old avatars and skip failed downloads in
 script/download

The cleanup step quoted its glob, so rm looked for a file literally
named *.png and stale avatars from a previous handles.txt stayed in the
montage. Unquote it, keeping avatars/.gitkeep.

curl also saved GitHub's 404 page as <handle>.png for a mistyped or
deleted handle, which made montage fail. Pass --fail, remove anything
a failed download left behind, and list the handles that failed.

Fixes #4.
---
 script/download | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/script/download b/script/download
index 3b1d786..41f51b9 100755
--- a/script/download
+++ b/script/download
@@ -4,9 +4,17 @@
 
 HANDLES=$(cat handles.txt)
 
-rm -Rf "./avatars/*.png"
+rm -f ./avatars/*.png
 
+FAILED=()
 for HANDLE in $HANDLES; do
   echo "Downloading avatar for $HANDLE"
-  curl -L -o "./avatars/$HANDLE.png" "https://github.com/$HANDLE.png"
-done
\ No newline at end of file
+  if ! curl -fL -o "./avatars/$HANDLE.png" "https://github.com/$HANDLE.png"; then
+    rm -f "./avatars/$HANDLE.png"
+    FAILED+=("$HANDLE")
+  fi
+done
+
+if [ ${#FAILED[@]} -gt 0 ]; then
+  echo "Couldn't download avatars for: ${FAILED[*]}" >&2
+fi
-- 
